    "key_finding": "A 82-parameter ephemeris-like basis can partially absorb a static synodic carrier on the real LLR sampling manifold (absorption 118.1% in the worst-case linear scenario). However, the dynamically modulated TEP signal's sideband-to-carrier ratio survives at 40.2% after fitting. On real INPOP19a residuals, the sideband-to-carrier ratio survives at 44.0%. The persistence of sideband structure \u2014 which requires explicit cross-frequency (annual \u00d7 synodic) terms that real ephemeris integrators do not include \u2014 demonstrates that the residual signal carries a genuine dynamical signature, not merely leakage from a partially absorbed static component. Moreover, the actual INPOP19a residuals exhibit \u03b7 = -4.53e-04, confirming that INPOP's own 100+ parameter fit did not absorb the signal, regardless of what an idealised linear basis might achieve in principle."
